{
  "id": "dark-coast-rescue",
  "name": "Dark Coast Rescue",
  "module": "dark-coast-tactical",
  "summary": "Port Ines has gone dark. Marines land on the western beach to find survivors and evacuate them to dropships waiting offshore.",
  "briefing": [
    "Port Ines, a coastal colony city of forty thousand, stopped transmitting thirty hours ago. Orbital imagery shows fires in the industrial district and movement in the streets, but no traffic and no lights.",
    "Your company lands at Beachhead Alpha on the western shore. Two heavy dropships, Halyard and Petrel, hold offshore. They can hover over open water but cannot safely fly inland. Every evacuee has to reach the beach.",
    "A distress beacon is active at St. Ines Hospital. Port authority staff were last heard from at the harbor. Treat everyone you meet as a survivor until you know otherwise.",
    "Success is measured in lives evacuated, not in contacts destroyed."
  ],
  "refereeNotes": "Outbreak origin is the marsh east of the city (suspected hive), with one brood nest already rooted beside it. A brute shelters in the industrial blocks south of the river, close to the landing. A screamer and crawlers hold the blocks around Central Precinct. Hordes drift toward noise and light. Raise the threat level as the operation goes on to unlock waves, monsters, and the Brood Mother. The school shelter and apartment block are unknown to players until scouted. Horde B is visible from the beach at start.",
